{ His king is racing back to stop your pawn. Only one road wins. }
1... Ke7 { He hurries home. Now find the square your king needs. } 2. Kb5 { Round the side! The pawn waits and the king goes first. [%csl Gb5] } (2. c6 { The pawn sets off alone, and that throws the win away. } 2... Kd6 { He steps in front on d6 and your king can never help. Drawn. }) (2. Kd5 { Straight ahead, and he simply takes the opposition. } 2... Kd7 { Now you cannot get past him. Only a draw. }) (2. Kb4 { The right idea, one square short. } 2... Kd7 { He is back in time and the win has slipped away. }) (2. Kd4 { A step backwards and the win is gone. } 2... Ke6 { He walks up to the pawn and holds it. Drawn. }) 2... Kd7 { He gets in front of the pawn. What now? } 3. Kb6 { The key square. Your pawn cannot be stopped any more. [%csl Gb6][%cal Gc5c8] } (3. c6+ { A check, and it costs you the win. } 3... Kc7 { He blocks on c7 and your pawn never moves again. Drawn. }) (3. Ka6 { Too far round, and the pawn is on its own. } 3... Kc6 { He walks up and the pawn falls. Drawn. }) (3. Ka5 { Sideways instead of forwards, and the win is gone. } 3... Kc6 { He reaches the pawn first. Drawn. }) (3. Kc4 { Backwards. He simply comes to the pawn. } 3... Kc6 { In front again, and you have nothing left. }) 1-0


