{ A new word: the square. His pawn will run, and your king must stay inside the box it draws. [%cal Ga4a8,Ga8e8,Ge8e4,Ge4a4] }
1. a5 { The pawn is off. The box runs a5 to a8 and across to d5 and d8. Step inside it. [%cal Ga5a8,Ga8d8,Gd8d5,Gd5a5][%cal Ye4d5] } 1... Kd5 { Inside the square, and now every push he makes keeps you there. [%csl Gd5] } (1... Kd4 { You are chasing the pawn instead of cutting it off. Count again. } 2. a6 Kc3 3. a7 { The box was one rank higher. That pawn queens and you are lost. [%csl Rc3][%cal Ra7a8,Ra8b8,Rb8b7,Rb7a7] }) (1... Ke5 { Sideways does nothing: the box does not move with you. [%csl Re5][%cal Ra5a8,Ra8d8,Rd8d5,Rd5a5] } 2. a6 Kd4 3. a7 { Two squares short. He queens next move. }) (1... Kd3 { Backwards, and the pawn is out of reach. } 2. a6 Kc2 3. a7 { It queens and you can only watch. }) 2. a6 { He pushes again and the box shrinks with him. Keep following. [%cal Ga6a8,Ga8c8,Gc8c6,Gc6a6][%cal Yd5c6] } 2... Kc6 { Still inside. Your king is walking the diagonal home. } (2... Kd6 { One step too slow, and you have left the box. [%csl Rd6][%cal Ra6a8,Ra8c8,Rc8c6,Rc6a6] } 3. a7 Kc5 4. a8=Q { The new queen arrives. You are lost. }) (2... Kc5 { The right column, the wrong rank. } 3. a7 Kb4 4. a8=Q { A move too late. }) (2... Kc4 { Down instead of across, and the box leaves you behind. [%csl Rc4][%cal Ra6a8,Ra8c8,Rc8c6,Rc6a6] } 3. a7 Kb3 4. a8=Q { Too slow by one move. }) 3. a7 { The last push. One more step and you meet the pawn at the corner. [%cal Ga7a8,Ga8b8,Gb8b7,Gb7a7][%cal Yc6b7] } 3... Kb7 { Caught it. The pawn can never queen and the game is drawn. [%csl Gb7][%cal Ga7a8,Ga8b8,Gb8b7,Gb7a7] } (3... Kb6 { So close. But b7 is the square that meets the pawn. } 4. a8=Q Kb5 { A whole queen against a bare king. Lost. }) (3... Kc7 { You need to stand right in front of it, on b7. } 4. a8=Q Kb6 { The pawn made it home. }) 0-1


