{ Two pawns each, and his king is a long way from all of them. One capture wins this. }
53. gxh4 { Take. It leaves one pawn each, and yours is the one with a king beside it. } (53. Kg4 { You walk round them, but the trade was the whole point. } 53... hxg3 54. Kxg3 Kg1 { One pawn each and neither can queen. Drawn. }) (53. g4 { Pushing past locks your own pawns up. } 53... Kg1 54. Ke2 Kg2 { His h pawn is the runner now and you are lost. }) (53. Ke4 { The king wanders off and the pawns are left alone. } 53... hxg3 54. Kf5 g2 { That pawn queens. You are lost. }) (53. Ke3 { Same problem: the trade was the whole idea. } 53... hxg3 54. Kd2 g2 { It queens next move. }) 53... gxh4 { He takes back. Now go and get it. } 54. Kg4 { Straight at the pawn. You take it next move and your own walks home. [%cal Gg4h4,Gh3h8] } (54. Kf4 { One square out, and his king arrives in time. } 54... Ke2 55. Ke4 Kd1 { He gets back to help and it is only a draw. }) (54. Ke3 { Backwards, and the h pawn is safe. } 54... Ke1 55. Kd3 Kd1 { Drawn. }) (54. Ke4 { Away from the pawn entirely. } 54... Ke1 55. Kd3 Kd1 { His king holds. Drawn. }) 1-0


