{ One more real game, and you are black. Every pawn move looks useful. Only one move wins. }
44. h4 { He grabs a little space on the wing. Now find the move. } 44... Ke5 { The king marches in. That e pawn cannot be defended twice. [%csl Ge4] } (44... c4 { You break on the queen side, and he just takes it. } 45. bxc4 h5 46. Kg3 Ke5 { Level. The king was the piece that had to move. }) (44... g5 { A pawn break when you have no time for one. } 45. hxg5+ Kxg5 46. Kf3 { His king reaches e4 and yours never does. You are losing. }) (44... d3 { Pushing your best pawn straight into his hands. } 45. cxd3 Ke5 46. Ke3 { The passer is gone and he holds everything. Lost. }) (44... h5 { A useful looking move, but the king had to go now. } 45. Ke2 c4 46. b4 { He gets his own passer running and you are losing. }) 45. Ke2 { He hurries across to hold the pawn. } 45... Kxe4 { Too late. The pawn falls and your d pawn becomes a monster. [%csl Gd4] } (45... c4 { Now this only helps him. } 46. bxc4 Kxe4 47. h5 { His h pawn runs and the win has gone. }) (45... g5 { Too late for pawn moves. } 46. hxg5 hxg5 47. Kd3 { His king reaches c4 and eats the queen side. Lost. }) (45... Kf4 { Walking past the pawn instead of taking it. } 46. Kd3 g6 47. Kc4 { He is into your pawns and you are the one losing. }) 0-1
